1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:02,120
But once we cross the finish line,

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,280
we won't be just friends anymore.

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,240
This is Ji from Class 7.

4
00:00:11,713 --> 00:00:13,313
He's here to help us out today.

5
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:14,540
Huh?

6
00:00:16,166 --> 00:00:17,293
Think about it.

7
00:00:17,573 --> 00:00:18,800
When did I start changing?

8
00:00:19,326 --> 00:00:20,326
Since when?

9
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:21,993
Not long after you did.

10
00:02:06,273 --> 00:02:08,680
It's time for the moment we've all been waiting for.

11
00:02:08,866 --> 00:02:12,013
The Best Actor award will be announced shortly.

12
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:13,893
Please stay tuned.

13
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:17,213
- Mom.
- Hmm?

14
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:18,350
BEST ACTOR AWARD 2010

15
00:02:18,386 --> 00:02:19,386
Do you want this?

16
00:02:19,913 --> 00:02:21,893
When I was just starting out in the industry,

17
00:02:22,186 --> 00:02:23,473
I really wanted this award.

18
00:02:25,486 --> 00:02:27,480
But now, I don't want it as much anymore.

19
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:31,353
Because now I have Khun, you, and Peach.

20
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,413
Oh, and your dad, too.

21
00:02:34,153 --> 00:02:35,473
I couldn't ask for anything more.

22
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:45,500
(I didn't know what I liked or wanted to do, )

23
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:47,926
(so I decided to enter the entertainment industry)

24
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,200
(to win that award for my mom.)

25
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:52,680
If you're interested, please contact me.

26
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:56,846
(Did you already say yes?)

27
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:58,626
Yes.

28
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,276
But you haven't signed a contract yet.

29
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:01,540
You can still change your mind.

30
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,320
You should enjoy being a kid while you can.

31
00:03:04,980 --> 00:03:06,420
Why are you in such a hurry to work?

32
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,866
Isn't what I've provided for you enough?

33
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:12,720
I want to make it on my own.

34
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:18,306
If you're determined to choose this path,

35
00:03:19,633 --> 00:03:21,630
then don't let me see you give up.

36
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:33,246
2013

37
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:42,620
You've been getting so many acting offers lately.

38
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:46,213
I don't understand why you'd want to
intern behind the scenes.

39
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,840
- Ta, I…
- How about this?

40
00:03:49,266 --> 00:03:52,346
Wait for the next project. It's a big one.

41
00:03:52,646 --> 00:03:54,713
If you get to work with this director,

42
00:03:54,746 --> 00:03:56,380
your future will be bright.

43
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,256
- You'll have plenty of roles to choose from.
- (But the more I did it, the more I realized)

44
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:03,680
- (I didn't enjoy being in front of the camera at all.)
- What do you want to do next?

45
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,293
Oh, hello, Ruth.

46
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,493
My handsome and kind brother,

47
00:04:20,973 --> 00:04:22,666
could you spoil the ending of the series for me?

48
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,900
Oh, honey.

49
00:04:23,933 --> 00:04:25,313
Give your brother a break.

50
00:04:28,690 --> 00:04:29,690
Are you okay, honey?

51
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,246
Yes, Mom.

52
00:04:31,533 --> 00:04:32,620
I just have a headache.

53
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,240
I guess I didn’t get enough sleep.

54
00:04:34,406 --> 00:04:37,226
Hmm, the series has wrapped filming.

55
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:38,380
You don't have to watch your weight anymore.

56
00:04:38,413 --> 00:04:39,413
Want some?

57
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,400
(After high school, )

58
00:04:43,053 --> 00:04:45,213
(we had basically disappeared from
each other's lives.)

59
00:04:47,210 --> 00:04:48,413
- Mom.
- Hmm?

60
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:51,393
Could you order this and have it delivered
to my condo?

61
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,420
Of course.

62
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:54,406
But we have to order from another shop.

63
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:57,426
Why is that?

64
00:04:57,793 --> 00:05:01,313
This is the last order my friend is taking.

65
00:05:01,420 --> 00:05:02,580
Her husband is seriously ill,

66
00:05:02,746 --> 00:05:04,226
so she's not making desserts anymore.

67
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,326
(Your mom's desserts)

68
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,866
(are the last thing connecting me to you.)

69
00:05:14,906 --> 00:05:16,226
(And they're about to disappear.)

70
00:05:17,870 --> 00:05:20,980
(But I still believed I had plenty of time)

71
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,300
(to get to know you all over again.)

72
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:25,260
(I’ll call you later, Ruth.)

73
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,920
(I have to go to the funeral.)

74
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:29,240
(I don't know how Mon and her children are doing.)

75
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,666
(I was filming overseas at the time.)

76
00:05:36,020 --> 00:05:37,540
(Even attending your father's funeral)

77
00:05:37,986 --> 00:05:39,186
(was something I couldn't do.)

78
00:05:43,066 --> 00:05:44,253
(All I knew was)

79
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,940
(that your sister and your mom had moved abroad.)

80
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:51,980
(As for you...)

81
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:54,666
(I never saw you again.)

82
00:05:56,890 --> 00:05:57,890
(Until...)

83
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:13,520
JIRAPHAT JAROENWONG
BORN: OCTOBER 31, 1993
DIED: MARCH 4, 2023

84
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:40,060
My dad really likes your work.

85
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:42,920
Uh...

86
00:06:43,006 --> 00:06:44,006
I'm Tyler.

87
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,360
Are you close to...

88
00:06:52,866 --> 00:06:54,240
Oh, no.

89
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,480
I haven't been in touch with Ji for a long time.

90
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:01,300
I'm only here because of Dennis.

91
00:07:02,650 --> 00:07:03,873
We work together.

92
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,366
He came to his wife's brother's funeral,

93
00:07:07,386 --> 00:07:08,960
so I came along.

94
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:11,520
Who would've thought

95
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:14,860
I'd end up attending the funeral of someone
I once knew?

96
00:07:41,990 --> 00:07:42,990
Ruth.

97
00:07:44,320 --> 00:07:45,320
Honey.

98
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:49,686
Why did you leave so soon?

99
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:51,700
Aren't you staying for the celebration?

100
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,280
I heard you're leaving the industry.

101
00:08:01,820 --> 00:08:03,373
Don't you have anything to say to me?

102
00:08:06,253 --> 00:08:07,253
Honey.

103
00:08:10,953 --> 00:08:12,160
If you don't, that’s fine.

104
00:08:13,590 --> 00:08:15,246
But if you ever need my help,

105
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,453
you can come talk to me.

106
00:08:29,586 --> 00:08:30,586
Ruth.

107
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,680
Ruth!

108
00:08:39,850 --> 00:08:40,962
Since you haven't been taking any jobs lately,

109
00:08:40,986 --> 00:08:42,153
you should see a doctor.

110
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,840
Do you hear me?

111
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,206
Here.

112
00:08:52,090 --> 00:08:53,893
What do you say, Tin?

113
00:08:54,413 --> 00:08:56,410
For you, Uncle Ri.

114
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:58,840
- Uncle Ruth.
- For Uncle Ruth.

115
00:08:59,386 --> 00:09:01,160
Ruth. Ruth Ata-a.

116
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:06,293
Ruth Atiwitch.

117
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,840
Ruth Ati…

118
00:09:09,066 --> 00:09:10,513
-Atee…
(-Hi, Tee.)

119
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:16,780
Tin, come here.

120
00:09:17,670 --> 00:09:21,106
Let’s see. What do you wanna eat?

121
00:09:37,310 --> 00:09:38,310
Sir.

122
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,253
This is an old bus stop.

123
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,040
Buses don't stop here anymore.

124
00:09:48,093 --> 00:09:49,093
Those roses…

125
00:09:50,470 --> 00:09:51,813
They’re beautiful.

126
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:54,366
- Are they for your lover?
- Ahh!

127
00:09:56,740 --> 00:09:58,380
There are frequent accidents around here.

128
00:09:58,826 --> 00:09:59,900
A lot of people have died.

129
00:10:00,153 --> 00:10:01,686
- You'd better be careful.
- Ah!

130
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:23,850
Ah!

131
00:10:39,686 --> 00:10:41,166
(When I opened my eyes, )

132
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,506
- (I realized...)
- Ji.

133
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:48,120
(I had traveled back in time.)

134
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,880
Jiraphat?

135
00:10:51,673 --> 00:10:52,753
And I got to see you again.

136
00:10:54,180 --> 00:10:56,233
Hold on. That’s all?

137
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,520
Mmm.

138
00:10:59,006 --> 00:11:02,833
When I woke up, you were there, staring at me.

139
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:07,093
So you don't remember anything

140
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:09,886
about what happened to you?

141
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,120
No.

142
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:14,860
I hadn't gotten checked out yet.

143
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,606
Do you still have headaches?

144
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:30,280
No.

145
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:32,393
After I got hit by the volleyball,

146
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:34,646
my dad took me to the hospital.

147
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:36,660
After that...

148
00:11:37,413 --> 00:11:38,653
Everything went back to normal.

149
00:11:39,213 --> 00:11:40,213
I wasn't in pain anymore.

150
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:43,466
It's because you don’t eat vegetables.

151
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,673
I'm not letting you pick them out anymore.

152
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:49,686
Don't make that face.

153
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,893
You still owe me an explanation.

154
00:11:58,066 --> 00:11:59,413
When did you find out about me?

155
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:00,820
Why did you tell me?

156
00:12:06,010 --> 00:12:07,010
Well…

157
00:12:08,150 --> 00:12:10,900
A few days after I got hit by the volleyball.

158
00:12:11,473 --> 00:12:13,186
(What should we do about Ms. Suda?)

159
00:12:13,613 --> 00:12:16,733
(We’re lucky Jiraphat could teach us instead.)

160
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,266
(And just like that, )

161
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,896
(Jiraphat, the good boy, lived his high school years)

162
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,120
(surrounded by his friends.)

163
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:28,013
(If it had been the old Jiraphat...)

164
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,042
- Mmm, there's an empty seat over there.
- (It wouldn't have been like that.)

165
00:12:31,066 --> 00:12:32,706
- Let’s ask him if we can sit there.
- Mm.

166
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:36,140
- Cheese!
- (Jiraphat, the good boy...)

167
00:12:36,253 --> 00:12:37,893
(went on school trips with his friends, )

168
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,480
(attended Science Day, )

169
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,226
(and took part in Sports Day.)

170
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:50,910
It took you half a year to realize?

171
00:12:53,100 --> 00:12:54,100
Sorry…

172
00:12:54,486 --> 00:12:55,486
Stop it.

173
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:06,160
Tyler came to my funeral, too?

174
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,040
And Kongpob.

175
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:13,560
What?

176
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:17,160
On the first day, while your aunt and sister

177
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,500
were still abroad,

178
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:22,080
Mr. Narong and my mom took care of
the funeral arrangements.

179
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,933
Kongpob, too.

180
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,100
Even though you two weren't close,

181
00:13:30,350 --> 00:13:31,870
Kongpob came to the funeral every day.

182
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,480
You must have been through a lot, huh?

183
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,120
Not really.

184
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:51,580
Maybe it's because I was a late bloomer.

185
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,620
Everything used to be difficult for me.

186
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:57,993
I wasn't good at socializing.

187
00:13:58,200 --> 00:13:59,990
I had trouble communicating with others.

188
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,413
So I chose to isolate myself.

189
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:07,206
Now that I've had another chance to live my life,

190
00:14:09,610 --> 00:14:11,450
things aren't as difficult as they used to be.

191
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:17,700
Besides...

192
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,000
I have you with me now.

193
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,680
I don't have to be afraid of anything anymore.

194
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,160
Since I'm not doing the school play anymore,

195
00:14:43,446 --> 00:14:45,526
why don't you come help out with
the student council?

196
00:14:45,846 --> 00:14:47,526
That way, we can spend more time together.

197
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,726
Wait, don't tell me...

198
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,560
You've joined the Drama Club, haven't you?

199
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:55,573
- Hey.
- Hey.

200
00:14:55,593 --> 00:14:56,786
- Hey.
- Where are you going?

201
00:14:57,380 --> 00:14:58,393
Why didn’t you tell me?

202
00:14:58,620 --> 00:15:00,390
Hmm, why didn’t you tell me? Hmm?

203
00:15:01,840 --> 00:15:03,926
- Why didn’t you tell me, hmm?
- It wasn’t my fault.

204
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,960
It's your fault.

205
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:07,153
If you'd told me from the beginning,

206
00:15:07,186 --> 00:15:09,313
I would've joined the student council.

207
00:15:09,513 --> 00:15:11,380
I wouldn't have said yes to Kwan.

208
00:15:34,333 --> 00:15:35,240
Ruth, Ji!

209
00:15:35,266 --> 00:15:36,266
Sh♪t.

210
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:38,630
Dinner’s ready.

211
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:40,500
Eh?

212
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,273
Ruth, what are you doing on the floor?

213
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:51,266
And why is Ji under the blanket?

214
00:15:53,500 --> 00:15:55,686
Uhm… he is cold.

215
00:15:55,900 --> 00:15:56,900
Right.

216
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:58,880
Cold?

217
00:15:59,933 --> 00:16:00,986
But it’s hot as hell.

218
00:16:02,750 --> 00:16:04,553
Peach, watch your language!

219
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:05,940
Oops.

220
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:08,320
Come down for dinner. Mom’s waiting.

221
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,073
Since we came here,

222
00:16:27,926 --> 00:16:29,406
I wonder what happened to that world.

223
00:16:30,993 --> 00:16:32,666
The people there would have to carry on.

224
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:34,940
They would have to get through it.

225
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:43,340
What do you think brought us here?

226
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:48,626
I don't know. Does it matter to you?

227
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,406
No. I'm just starting to feel a bit scared.

228
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,560
Don’t be afraid.

229
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,280
From now on,

230
00:17:10,213 --> 00:17:11,213
wherever you go,

231
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:12,906
I’ll go with you.

232
00:17:22,030 --> 00:17:24,213
(Ruth, Ji, aren’t you done yet?)

233
00:17:24,246 --> 00:17:25,753
(Come down for dinner!)

234
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:28,540
But right now,

235
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:30,660
we should be having dinner.

236
00:17:31,410 --> 00:17:32,410
I think so.

237
00:17:34,186 --> 00:17:36,180
“He is cold.” It’s hot as hell.

238
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:46,980
This one?

239
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:49,820
Can you do it?

240
00:17:49,853 --> 00:17:50,853
In one bite.

241
00:17:52,326 --> 00:17:53,413
Ploy, hold on.

242
00:17:53,666 --> 00:17:55,113
- It’s too cold.
- Eat it!

243
00:17:58,050 --> 00:17:59,050
Wait a second.

244
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,020
Did you get a free one?

245
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:06,220
Ugh.

246
00:18:06,766 --> 00:18:07,766
Too bad.

247
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,433
Hey! I got it!

248
00:18:13,473 --> 00:18:14,033
I got it!

249
00:18:14,034 --> 00:18:16,030
Actors, the rehearsal starts in 10 minutes.

250
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,146
Can I go get my free popsicle first?

251
00:18:18,366 --> 00:18:19,886
Before the shop closes. I'll be quick.

252
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,653
- I’ll go, too.
- Hey, wait.

253
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:30,140
Are you almost done?

254
00:18:30,726 --> 00:18:32,166
They still have two more rehearsals.

255
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:33,396
Do you want to go home first?

256
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:35,040
Mmm, nah, I can wait.

257
00:18:38,970 --> 00:18:40,880
Why don’t you join our club?

258
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:42,280
Hmm?

259
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:44,280
Right.

260
00:18:44,526 --> 00:18:46,620
Since you're already waiting for Ji and Tyler,

261
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:48,850
why not put your free time to good use?

262
00:18:49,430 --> 00:18:50,590
You'll get more credits, too.

263
00:18:54,966 --> 00:18:55,966
Hmm, I'll give it a try.

264
00:19:01,033 --> 00:19:02,040
Hi, How can I help?

265
00:19:15,846 --> 00:19:16,846
- Here!
- Oh.

266
00:19:21,090 --> 00:19:22,993
Didn't you ask me to be the club treasurer?

267
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,876
Do I really need to stay and watch rehearsals?

268
00:19:24,900 --> 00:19:26,022
You should. If you're not here,

269
00:19:26,046 --> 00:19:28,600
who's going to keep Tyler in check?

270
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:32,220
Tyler may be like this,

271
00:19:32,460 --> 00:19:34,220
but he's more reliable than you think.

272
00:19:37,070 --> 00:19:41,613
But it's okay if you don't want to stay.

273
00:19:42,840 --> 00:19:45,060
If you want to be with the president, you can go.

274
00:19:46,350 --> 00:19:47,873
I'll call you if I need you.

275
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:49,520
It's fine.

276
00:19:50,026 --> 00:19:51,386
The air conditioning is nice here.

277
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,700
It's cooler than the student council room.

278
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,260
Besides...

279
00:19:59,140 --> 00:20:01,260
I want to try working with my clubmates for a change.

280
00:20:03,986 --> 00:20:05,766
Woo!

281
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,233
Super Tyler is here!!

282
00:20:08,253 --> 00:20:09,520
Super Tyler.

283
00:20:09,566 --> 00:20:11,080
Super Tyler.

284
00:20:11,106 --> 00:20:12,460
Super Tyler.

285
00:20:12,493 --> 00:20:13,493
Woohoo!

286
00:20:13,686 --> 00:20:14,686
Tyler!

287
00:20:14,820 --> 00:20:15,820
Don’t play with that.

288
00:20:16,070 --> 00:20:17,553
Woo!

289
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:18,560
Tyler!

290
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:23,586
Okay, okay.

291
00:20:23,613 --> 00:20:24,613
Kongpob.

292
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:26,986
Which one do you think looks better?

293
00:20:27,006 --> 00:20:28,906
I feel like I like both.

294
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,766
- Should we use both then?
- Mmm.

295
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:36,813
Even if they're not historically accurate,

296
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:39,420
the costumes should still match.

297
00:20:39,893 --> 00:20:41,880
One is elaborate, while the other is simple.

298
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,220
They look like they're from different eras.

299
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:46,766
I think the first one is better.

300
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,520
It'll stand out more on stage.

301
00:20:58,130 --> 00:20:59,130
- Romeo!
- Juliet!

302
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:02,080
Ji.

303
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:03,609
Who's supposed to speak first?

304
00:21:03,633 --> 00:21:05,460
Juliet has to wait for Romeo to speak first.

305
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:06,920
Sorry.

306
00:21:07,273 --> 00:21:07,993
My bad.

307
00:21:08,013 --> 00:21:09,013
It's okay.

308
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:11,593
By the way, how's this scene?

309
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:12,920
This scene is good.

310
00:21:13,153 --> 00:21:14,626
But if I had to change something,

311
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,860
Romeo needs to speak with more emotion.

312
00:21:18,390 --> 00:21:21,366
I want it to feel like Romeo is truly

313
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,900
in love with Juliet.

314
00:21:23,933 --> 00:21:25,742
Also, Juliet keeps accidentally saying Tyler's name.

315
00:21:25,766 --> 00:21:26,793
Be careful with that.

316
00:21:27,740 --> 00:21:28,740
Okay.

317
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,696
Then... shall we rehearse one more time?

318
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:31,086
Okay.

319
00:21:31,266 --> 00:21:32,666
You've rehearsed a lot already.

320
00:21:32,693 --> 00:21:33,586
You can take a break.

321
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:34,620
That's a good idea, Ji.

322
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:36,380
I'm really, really hungry.

323
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,080
I'll be right back.

324
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:40,360
Yo, Ruth!

325
00:21:44,050 --> 00:21:44,480
Hi.

326
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,040
Hi.

327
00:21:58,640 --> 00:22:00,500
Don't you have anything to say?

328
00:22:02,966 --> 00:22:04,960
You're so good. There's nothing I need to say.

329
00:22:06,070 --> 00:22:07,070
That's not true.

330
00:22:07,540 --> 00:22:08,746
There are only two weeks left.

331
00:22:08,766 --> 00:22:10,686
I don't know if we'll finish rehearsing in time.

332
00:22:11,080 --> 00:22:13,333
Did you finish rehearsing in time back then?

333
00:22:15,610 --> 00:22:18,666
I finished learning my lines before New Year's.

334
00:22:21,106 --> 00:22:22,640
Oh, wow.

335
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,673
Don't worry.

336
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,600
Just keep at it, and it'll get done.

337
00:22:33,480 --> 00:22:34,480
Is it good?

338
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,190
Mmm, it's delicious.

339
00:22:37,470 --> 00:22:38,870
You've got something on your mouth.

340
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,880
Where?

341
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,160
Mr. President.

342
00:22:52,860 --> 00:22:54,580
Why aren’t you at the student council room?

343
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:56,200
What are you doing in the Drama Club?

344
00:22:58,640 --> 00:22:59,733
Why can’t I be here?

345
00:23:00,610 --> 00:23:02,993
If you're here to help us, that's fine.

346
00:23:03,013 --> 00:23:04,500
But if you're here to take Ji away,

347
00:23:04,913 --> 00:23:05,913
I won't allow it.

348
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,280
Ji belongs to the Drama Club.

349
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:13,900
This meeting room is... pretty convenient.

350
00:23:14,906 --> 00:23:16,900
The performance is only two weeks away.

351
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:18,900
If the Drama Club didn't have a room to use...

352
00:23:19,280 --> 00:23:20,520
you'd be in a tough spot.

353
00:23:24,370 --> 00:23:25,873
Girl Kwan, Ms. Mai wants to see you.

354
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:40,140
Hey, you're abusing your power as club president.

355
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:44,113
I’m just a kid.

356
00:23:54,290 --> 00:23:57,146
Is Ploy gonna be okay?

357
00:23:58,390 --> 00:24:00,533
She's studying for exams and memorizing
her lines.

358
00:24:01,126 --> 00:24:02,366
She's pushing herself too hard.

359
00:24:04,850 --> 00:24:05,866
She'll be fine.

360
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,893
You're in the same class.

361
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:11,440
You should remind her to take it easy.

362
00:24:12,330 --> 00:24:14,893
I'm back, everyone!

363
00:24:15,526 --> 00:24:17,653
I brought fruit and shumai.

364
00:24:18,266 --> 00:24:19,266
Let’s eat.

365
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:20,360
Come on.

366
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:22,713
Wait for me.

367
00:24:22,740 --> 00:24:23,740
Wow.

368
00:24:25,340 --> 00:24:25,900
Can I eat now?

369
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:27,440
Go on. Eat up.

370
00:24:28,230 --> 00:24:29,230
See?

371
00:24:29,533 --> 00:24:30,660
I told you it’ll be fine.

372
00:24:36,340 --> 00:24:37,900
Ji, Ruth, come on.

373
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:38,940
Before it’s all gone.

374
00:24:53,193 --> 00:24:54,193
Wow.

375
00:24:54,980 --> 00:24:57,373
Did you perform on a stage this big last time?

376
00:24:58,480 --> 00:24:59,480
Mmm.

377
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,640
Ji, have you seen Tyler?

378
00:25:03,490 --> 00:25:04,490
Tyler?

379
00:25:04,813 --> 00:25:07,046
He said he was tired from carrying the set.

380
00:25:07,273 --> 00:25:08,833
So he asked to go get something to eat.

381
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:10,180
President,

382
00:25:10,213 --> 00:25:11,793
When will Ploy finish her lab exam?

383
00:25:12,270 --> 00:25:15,586
Mmm, probably in another 15 minutes.

384
00:25:17,670 --> 00:25:18,746
That's too long to wait.

385
00:25:19,113 --> 00:25:20,740
We only have the auditorium for an hour.

386
00:25:21,233 --> 00:25:22,953
We won't have time to rehearse every scene.

387
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:26,546
Then, Ji and President,

388
00:25:26,573 --> 00:25:28,156
could you go put on your mics and
rehearse the lines?

389
00:25:28,180 --> 00:25:30,036
Go on stage and act as if you're performing for real.

390
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:32,060
That way, we can check the sound and lighting too.

391
00:25:32,330 --> 00:25:34,953
I don’t mind, but...

392
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:36,360
Let's do it.

393
00:25:36,860 --> 00:25:38,220
But I want to be Romeo.

394
00:25:38,986 --> 00:25:40,413
That's the spirit!

395
00:25:40,546 --> 00:25:41,746
You two finally helped us out.

396
00:25:42,590 --> 00:25:44,746
Now, go put on your mics backstage.

397
00:25:45,073 --> 00:25:46,186
Perform the balcony scene.

398
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:00,880
Are you nervous?

399
00:26:03,170 --> 00:26:04,170
No.

400
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:06,400
It just feels like seeing an old friend again.

401
00:26:10,470 --> 00:26:11,886
I've memorized all my lines.

402
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:14,173
Do you want to go over yours again?

403
00:26:16,760 --> 00:26:17,760
That's not necessary.

404
00:26:20,500 --> 00:26:22,273
If the actors are ready, let's begin.

405
00:26:42,490 --> 00:26:44,660
Romeo, do you love me?

406
00:26:46,150 --> 00:26:47,150
Dear Juliet,

407
00:26:47,593 --> 00:26:48,913
I swear by the moon.

408
00:26:56,140 --> 00:26:57,606
The moon changes every day.

409
00:26:58,353 --> 00:26:59,566
Do not swear by the moon.

410
00:27:02,330 --> 00:27:03,713
Then what should I swear by?

411
00:27:05,280 --> 00:27:08,080
What kind of satisfaction can you expect tonight?

412
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,673
Then I will not say anything

413
00:27:36,670 --> 00:27:37,886
I will stand by you,

414
00:27:39,880 --> 00:27:40,933
hold your hand,

415
00:27:44,320 --> 00:27:45,733
and never let you go again

416
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:07,893
Everyone!

417
00:28:09,180 --> 00:28:10,960
Tyler's back!

418
00:28:12,090 --> 00:28:15,286
I bought steamed buns and snacks for everyone.

419
00:28:20,306 --> 00:28:21,306
Snacks.

420
00:28:24,750 --> 00:28:26,293
We thought the mic was malfunctioning.

421
00:28:26,553 --> 00:28:28,433
You should've told me before turning yours off.

422
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:31,826
Hurry up and eat.

423
00:28:31,853 --> 00:28:33,533
We still have time for one more rehearsal.

424
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Yeah.

425
00:28:37,046 --> 00:28:39,106
We'll have to rehearse with the whole cast later.

426
00:28:39,473 --> 00:28:40,873
We probably won't have enough mics.

427
00:28:42,400 --> 00:28:44,466
I hope it won't be too much trouble for you, right?

428
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:50,060
I'll go get them.

429
00:28:50,186 --> 00:28:51,573
Hey, I'll go with you.

430
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:10,586
Are there microphones here? It's so dusty.

431
00:29:23,370 --> 00:29:24,370
What?

432
00:29:25,810 --> 00:29:27,026
Was I good today?

433
00:29:27,533 --> 00:29:28,533
Good? How?

434
00:29:28,580 --> 00:29:29,320
You messed up your lines.

435
00:29:29,340 --> 00:29:30,420
You couldn't remember them.

436
00:29:31,020 --> 00:29:32,173
And what was that ending?

437
00:29:33,226 --> 00:29:34,260
It was so cheesy.

438
00:29:37,910 --> 00:29:38,910
Cheesy?

439
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,493
But I saw Juliet smiling.

440
00:29:44,190 --> 00:29:46,093
And his ears were red too.

441
00:29:48,393 --> 00:29:50,390
What? Let's keep looking.

442
00:29:53,870 --> 00:29:54,870
You know...

443
00:29:55,313 --> 00:29:58,300
There are two legends about this room.

444
00:30:05,990 --> 00:30:08,033
If it's a ghost story, don't tell me.

445
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:13,240
Then there's only one legend left to tell.

446
00:30:16,370 --> 00:30:17,370
Let's hear it.

447
00:30:21,220 --> 00:30:22,306
They say...

448
00:30:22,966 --> 00:30:26,593
Anyone who confesses their love in this room will have their feelings returned.

449
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:33,320
How could anyone find love in
a creepy room like this?

450
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:37,593
Besides, is there anything else you need
to confess to me?

451
00:30:39,780 --> 00:30:40,780
Nothing else.

452
00:30:41,346 --> 00:30:43,713
You already know everything about me.

453
00:30:46,260 --> 00:30:48,060
Stop saying such cheesy things.

454
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,486
Actually, there's another legend.

455
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:01,280
What legend?

456
00:31:01,646 --> 00:31:02,726
When did it happen?

457
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:05,300
Just now.

458
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:09,120
Tell me.

459
00:31:11,590 --> 00:31:12,726
They say...

460
00:31:13,340 --> 00:31:14,720
Anyone who makes a wish in here

461
00:31:15,660 --> 00:31:16,660
will have it come true.

462
00:31:20,620 --> 00:31:23,880
What does this little boy wish for, then?

463
00:31:26,990 --> 00:31:28,550
I want to do what we did on Sports Day.

464
00:31:32,850 --> 00:31:33,960
Eating red sausages?

465
00:31:36,373 --> 00:31:39,680
I'm sorry, but I don't think you'll get your wish today.

466
00:32:07,620 --> 00:32:08,973
Atiwitch, Jiraphat.

467
00:32:12,660 --> 00:32:14,786
You two, come with me.

468
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:31,320
Don't worry.

469
00:32:34,580 --> 00:32:36,173
I really didn't get my wish.

470
00:32:37,473 --> 00:32:39,326
I knew these legends weren’t reliable.

471
00:32:43,510 --> 00:32:45,066
(Do you two know)

472
00:32:45,830 --> 00:32:47,180
why I called you here?

473
00:32:56,200 --> 00:32:57,606
If you won't say anything,

474
00:32:58,480 --> 00:32:59,686
then I'll say it myself.

475
00:33:04,200 --> 00:33:06,720
The storage room is a public space.

476
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,846
And it's located on school grounds.

477
00:33:11,690 --> 00:33:12,690
Am I right?

478
00:33:15,250 --> 00:33:16,250
Yes, sir.

479
00:33:22,580 --> 00:33:23,580
Yes, sir.

480
00:33:23,900 --> 00:33:25,646
Even though it's an old room,

481
00:33:27,920 --> 00:33:29,733
people still pass by all the time.

482
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:34,266
More importantly, it's not your private space.

483
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:38,220
Think carefully before you do anything.

484
00:33:39,640 --> 00:33:41,000
Do you understand what I'm saying?

485
00:33:42,890 --> 00:33:43,890
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

486
00:33:45,560 --> 00:33:48,186
All right. For the two of you,

487
00:33:49,540 --> 00:33:51,116
I'll let you off with just a warning this time.

488
00:33:51,140 --> 00:33:53,020
But don't let it happen again.

489
00:33:54,380 --> 00:33:55,380
Yes, sir.

490
00:34:00,433 --> 00:34:02,426
Hey, why are you still standing there?

491
00:34:02,870 --> 00:34:03,886
Go back.

492
00:34:03,926 --> 00:34:04,926
Well...

493
00:34:06,070 --> 00:34:07,070
Is that all?

494
00:34:07,100 --> 00:34:08,006
That's all.

495
00:34:08,040 --> 00:34:09,040
What else do you want?

496
00:34:09,140 --> 00:34:11,606
Or would you like to pick up trash
in the bushes again, huh?

497
00:34:12,230 --> 00:34:13,230
No, sir.

498
00:34:13,386 --> 00:34:14,073
It's just...

499
00:34:14,240 --> 00:34:17,866
Or do you want me to make you two break up?

500
00:34:21,620 --> 00:34:22,646
Separate you.

501
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,920
Make sure you never see each other again.

502
00:34:26,020 --> 00:34:27,280
If I did that,

503
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:30,853
I'd have to make every couple in
this school break up too.

504
00:34:31,780 --> 00:34:32,833
I'd be exhausted.

505
00:34:36,850 --> 00:34:39,273
Do your families know about this yet?

506
00:34:43,440 --> 00:34:44,440
Not yet, sir.

507
00:34:44,946 --> 00:34:46,386
Atiwitch, yours doesn't know either?

508
00:34:48,926 --> 00:34:51,206
If your families found out,
do you think they'd accept it?

509
00:34:55,100 --> 00:34:57,140
Uh... I'm not sure, sir.

510
00:34:57,680 --> 00:35:02,306
If you want me to talk to your families,
just let me know.

511
00:35:03,470 --> 00:35:04,470
But remember,

512
00:35:05,186 --> 00:35:07,313
if your families kick you out,

513
00:35:08,100 --> 00:35:09,680
come see me at my boxing gym.

514
00:35:10,780 --> 00:35:12,300
You can lie around and relax,

515
00:35:13,080 --> 00:35:15,493
or punch the heavy bags to let off some steam.

516
00:35:16,660 --> 00:35:18,020
My boxing gym is the safest place.

517
00:35:20,100 --> 00:35:21,100
Do you understand?

518
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:26,720
Yes, sir.

519
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:40,480
Aren't you going to let go of my hand?

520
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:43,480
No.

521
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:45,200
I'm not letting go.

522
00:35:47,870 --> 00:35:50,180
Wow, you two took so long to find the mics.

523
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:51,840
Kwan's been complaining nonstop.

524
00:35:51,913 --> 00:35:53,713
Sorry, something came up.

525
00:35:58,150 --> 00:35:59,440
But it's okay.

526
00:35:59,460 --> 00:36:01,653
Tyler already got the mics.

527
00:36:01,900 --> 00:36:03,650
We're done rehearsing now.

528
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:06,373
We’re taking the costumes to Kongpob's
house to work on them.

529
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:08,653
Yeah, there's plenty of space at the boxing gym.

530
00:36:08,680 --> 00:36:09,726
There are lots of boxers there too,

531
00:36:09,740 --> 00:36:10,780
so I can ask them to help.

532
00:36:10,973 --> 00:36:12,886
You guys are welcome to come along.

533
00:36:12,926 --> 00:36:14,280
Okay, we'll catch up with you.

534
00:36:15,080 --> 00:36:16,080
Let's go.

535
00:36:22,080 --> 00:36:25,346
Should we get our bags and head home?

536
00:36:28,210 --> 00:36:29,720
Can I have dinner at your place?

537
00:36:30,620 --> 00:36:32,500
What if I say no?

538
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:35,686
Then I'll tell your mom you won't let me come over.

539
00:36:37,100 --> 00:36:38,506
That's cheating.

540
00:36:40,250 --> 00:36:41,740
Fine. Let’s go.

541
00:36:50,660 --> 00:36:54,100
You looked really strong when you played volleyball.

542
00:36:55,270 --> 00:36:56,270
That's your friend.

543
00:36:56,420 --> 00:36:57,420
Shhh!

544
00:37:00,340 --> 00:37:02,153
When you ran away from Mr. Narong...

545
00:37:02,746 --> 00:37:04,386
Oh, no!

546
00:37:04,420 --> 00:37:06,193
I'm sorry, sir. I'm sorry!

547
00:37:06,353 --> 00:37:07,353
Tyler!

548
00:37:09,813 --> 00:37:11,040
You looked so cool.

549
00:37:13,300 --> 00:37:15,033
And then...

550
00:37:18,560 --> 00:37:19,906
Here, take this.

551
00:37:22,270 --> 00:37:23,533
(You gave me your umbrella)

552
00:37:24,660 --> 00:37:26,353
(while you ran in the rain yourself.)

553
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:31,260
You bought shumai and steamed buns
for everyone in the club,

554
00:37:31,633 --> 00:37:34,073
because you knew Kwan was the only one
who didn't get a break.

555
00:37:35,180 --> 00:37:36,500
You were so sweet.

556
00:37:38,520 --> 00:37:39,766
I really like you.

557
00:37:44,860 --> 00:37:45,860
But...

558
00:37:46,146 --> 00:37:47,680
I don't feel that way about you, Ploy.

559
00:37:51,070 --> 00:37:52,070
Wow.

560
00:37:53,500 --> 00:37:54,580
That really hurts.

561
00:37:56,050 --> 00:37:57,953
Damn these storage room legends.

562
00:38:06,980 --> 00:38:08,406
Anyway, thank you

563
00:38:09,230 --> 00:38:10,446
for being honest with me.

564
00:38:11,870 --> 00:38:14,380
And don't worry about the school play.

565
00:38:14,860 --> 00:38:15,860
I can separate the two.

566
00:38:15,986 --> 00:38:16,666
I'm not worried.

567
00:38:16,960 --> 00:38:18,040
I know you're the best.

568
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:23,293
How could you say that to someone
you just broke the heart of, huh?

569
00:38:24,293 --> 00:38:25,453
I don't like you anymore.

570
00:38:26,640 --> 00:38:27,640
See you around.

571
00:38:27,820 --> 00:38:28,820
I'm off.

572
00:38:29,226 --> 00:38:30,226
Bye-bye.

573
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:44,200
Hi, Ji. Hi, Ruth.

574
00:38:45,190 --> 00:38:47,666
Have you been on a secret date?

575
00:38:51,706 --> 00:38:53,306
Why are you looking at me like that, Ji?

576
00:38:55,230 --> 00:38:57,093
Are you sure about letting her go?

577
00:38:59,220 --> 00:39:00,666
Do you want me to follow her?

578
00:39:03,860 --> 00:39:06,606
You two have to go back to get your bags, right?

579
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:09,460
Could you take this to Kwan for me?

580
00:39:10,260 --> 00:39:11,353
I'm off. See you on Monday.

581
00:39:11,633 --> 00:39:12,633
Good luck.

582
00:39:18,340 --> 00:39:20,946
Your friend is colder than I thought.

583
00:39:23,290 --> 00:39:25,513
No, he's actually the opposite.

584
00:39:27,773 --> 00:39:29,770
If I told you to cry in front of me,

585
00:39:30,066 --> 00:39:31,066
would you?

586
00:39:33,990 --> 00:39:35,606
- No.
- Why not?

587
00:39:36,093 --> 00:39:38,853
Am I not special enough for you to cry
in front of me?

588
00:39:38,906 --> 00:39:39,906
That's not it.

589
00:39:40,860 --> 00:39:42,126
- But...
- Exactly.

590
00:39:42,746 --> 00:39:44,673
You and Ploy have one thing in common

591
00:39:47,350 --> 00:39:49,666
You're both perfectionists.

592
00:39:52,220 --> 00:39:54,786
Tyler asked us to take this to the auditorium instead

593
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:58,640
because he wanted to give Ploy some space
so she wouldn't feel embarrassed.

594
00:39:59,420 --> 00:40:03,220
Someone like that isn't cold at all.

595
00:40:08,580 --> 00:40:09,580
Why are you smiling?

596
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:14,233
I'm just happy to have you.

597
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,080
You’re being cheesy again.

598
00:40:21,880 --> 00:40:23,240
But your ears are red.

599
00:40:26,440 --> 00:40:27,440
Let’s get back.

600
00:40:31,233 --> 00:40:35,473
VEGETABLE AND FLOWER GARDEN PLOT
HOME ECONOMICS

601
00:40:35,506 --> 00:40:37,673
Why do I have to deal with

602
00:40:37,713 --> 00:40:40,346
the students in your classes?

603
00:40:40,373 --> 00:40:41,446
I don't understand.

604
00:40:41,626 --> 00:40:42,686
Please, Mr. Rong.

605
00:40:43,133 --> 00:40:45,406
You said we should help each other.

606
00:40:45,626 --> 00:40:49,300
My students are your students too now.

607
00:40:49,506 --> 00:40:51,093
That's right, Mr. Narong.

608
00:40:51,273 --> 00:40:53,360
Let's help keep an eye on the students together.

609
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:54,560
Yeah?

610
00:40:55,106 --> 00:40:56,406
You two seem to get along well.

611
00:40:56,873 --> 00:40:57,893
Are you dating?

612
00:40:58,370 --> 00:41:00,753
Oh, God. Don't even start.

613
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,060
You should ask him.

614
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:07,240
Why?

615
00:41:08,130 --> 00:41:12,766
Back in 11th grade, I almost confessed
my feelings to him.

616
00:41:13,153 --> 00:41:16,500
But before I could, Tin rejected me first.

617
00:41:16,780 --> 00:41:18,940
He said he already had someone he liked.

618
00:41:19,326 --> 00:41:20,746
Oops. Ouch.

619
00:41:21,586 --> 00:41:22,586
Mr. Tin...

620
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:24,760
But it's okay.

621
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:27,773
I'd say we're even now,

622
00:41:28,186 --> 00:41:29,900
since we both got our hearts broken.

623
00:41:30,406 --> 00:41:31,453
He deserved it.

624
00:41:39,970 --> 00:41:41,580
You’re good at riding a bike now, Tee.

625
00:41:41,626 --> 00:41:43,353
You used to ride on the back of mine.

626
00:41:44,080 --> 00:41:44,780
I've grown up now.

627
00:41:45,033 --> 00:41:46,320
I’m not your Tee anymore.

628
00:41:47,113 --> 00:41:48,113
Fine.

629
00:41:48,160 --> 00:41:49,280
I’ll call you Ruth.

630
00:41:50,100 --> 00:41:51,100
Just Ruth?

631
00:41:52,206 --> 00:41:53,206
President Ruth.

632
00:41:53,620 --> 00:41:54,620
No.

633
00:41:55,286 --> 00:41:56,286
Oh, please.

634
00:41:58,390 --> 00:41:59,390
My Ruth.

635
00:42:01,330 --> 00:42:02,330
Yes?

636
00:42:05,906 --> 00:42:08,416
(In a world where we don’t get the chance to go back and make things right...)

637
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:09,440
Can you do this?

638
00:42:09,830 --> 00:42:11,986
Mmm, I think so.

639
00:42:12,353 --> 00:42:14,006
What are you doing? I’ll show you.

640
00:42:14,040 --> 00:42:15,346
Pull it up.

641
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:17,486
- Like this.
- Okay.

642
00:42:17,526 --> 00:42:18,526
You got it?

643
00:42:19,650 --> 00:42:21,166
(There are still people struggling, )

644
00:42:21,486 --> 00:42:22,553
(trying to protect)

645
00:42:22,700 --> 00:42:24,640
(and hold on to what they have left)

646
00:42:31,590 --> 00:42:33,760
(so they won't have to suffer another loss.)

647
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:18,360
I’m dating someone.

648
00:43:18,513 --> 00:43:20,860
Who are you dating, Ji?

649
00:43:22,240 --> 00:43:23,793
See you tomorrow.

650
00:43:31,613 --> 00:43:33,306
Maybe your dad is not that strict.

651
00:43:36,420 --> 00:43:37,420
Sh♪t!

652
00:43:38,153 --> 00:43:39,253
I’m glad I have you.
